#Understanding each field

1. Address
This is the IPv4 address of a device on the local network.
The system uses ARP to resolve this IP to a MAC address before sending Ethernet frames.

192.168.56.1: VirtualBox host-only adapter gateway.

10.0.2.3: VirtualBox DNS server.

_gateway: Default gateway 
	  10.0.2.2 in your case

192.168.56.100: Another host on the host-only network.

2. HWtype (Hardware Type)

Indicates the hardware protocol type.
ether means Ethernet
It tells the system what type of Layer 2 address format is being used.

3. HWaddress

This is the MAC address corresponding to the IP address.
It is a 48-bit physical hardware address.
Used at Layer 2 to deliver Ethernet frames.

4. Flags

This indicates the status of the ARP entry.

C: Complete
The ARP resolution was successful. The MAC address is known.
M: Permanent entry 
   manually added

P: Published entry

?: Incomplete.The MAC is not resolved yet

5. Mask

Rarely used in modern systems.
In the past it was used for proxy ARP or subnet masking.

6. Iface (Interface)

Indicates which network interface learned this ARP entry.
ARP entries are stored per interface because ARP works only within a local broadcast domain.
